<!--
Trimmed sample of https://alertingauthority.wmo.int/rss.xml, captured
18 Aug 2026. Real entries, not synthesized; see docs/DATA-SOURCES.md's
"WMO Register of Alerting Authorities" section for how this was pulled.

Covers the cases the join problem needs:
  * Nigeria (NGA to ng): raa:authorityAbbrev "nma" disagrees with SWIC's
    "nimet"; proves authority-level matching cannot be reconstructed.
  * USA (USA to us), NOAA/NWS: abbrev "noaa" happens to agree with our
    "us-noaa" source id, the one case where a naive join would work,
    which is exactly why it is dangerous to generalise from it.
  * Germany (DEU to de): a country we do not carry any alerts for.
  * South Africa (ZAF to za), United Kingdom (GBR to gb): more alpha-3
    round-trip cases for the mapping table test.
  * EUMETNET (EUM): not a country at all, an alpha-3 the embedded
    table cannot and should not map. Proves unmappable codes surface
    rather than vanish.
  * Saint Vincent and the Grenadines / Caribbean Meteorological
    Organization: one of the 3 real entries in the live register with
    no raa:authorityAbbrev at all.
-->
